Project structure overview

- apps/: application code and domain logic (e.g., web UI, projector handlers, game-server rooms)
- packages/: infrastructure-only shared libraries (e.g., db schema, http utils, rate limit, ids)
- infra/: deployment/runtime infra (docker, cloudflared, postgres, scripts). No app code.

Domain boundary guidance

- Keep every bounded context self-contained inside its app (`apps/web/src/lib/server/<context>`, `apps/projector/src/handlers/<context>`, etc.).
- Do **not** place domain code (aggregates, event types, projections, room logic) in packages/.
- `packages/*` must stay generic/infra. Only primitives that make sense across all contexts should live there.
- When adding new capabilities:
  1. Extend the domain module inside the owning app.
  2. Expose it through adapters (routes, handlers) in the same app.
  3. Touch packages only if you need reusable infra helpers.

See `/README.md` for more details.